    "m_ObjectId": "f6bbd8d7c53546949ed3b4cb23cb2853",
    "m_Title": "Sprite Wind",
    "m_Content": "Moves the top of a sprite card sideways; the feet stay still.\nOffset = Direction x sway x height x Strength.\n- Height: object-space Y above the pivot (the feet), never below 0. Taller cards sway further.\n- Sway: sin(time x Speed + phase) + 0.5 x sin(2.3 x time x Speed + 1.7 x phase), between -1.5 and +1.5,\n  so the top moves at most 1.5 x Strength x height.\n- Phase: (world X + world Z of the object) x Frequency. Higher Frequency = neighbouring plants move less in step.\n- Direction is in world space. An empty (0,0,0) direction falls back to (1,0,0).\n- Time is game time, so the wind stops when the game is paused.",
